--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn input file: IEA-15MW on the UMaine VolturnUS-S semi-submersible (OpenFAST, CompMooring = 5)
CableDyn is its own module. Each line is one sectioned line object: a LINE
runs End A (fairlead side) -> End B (anchor side) through ordered SECTIONS, each with its
own line type, unstretched length, and mesh. The initial condition is a Newton static
equilibrium (no dynamic relaxation and no relaxation tuning), and dynamics are implicit
generalised-alpha. In coupled use the host owns the environment (gravity, water density,
water depth) and the marching clock; the OPTIONS section below carries only CableDyn's own
solver settings and the seabed contact parameters. Output channels use the FairTen/AnchTen
vocabulary; requested channels are printed at static equilibrium and written to .out/.outb.
--------------------------- LINE TYPES ----------------------------------------
Name  Diam   Mass    EA       BA    EI    Cdn   Cdt   Can   Cat
(-)   (m)    (kg/m)  (N)      (-)   (Nm2) (-)   (-)   (-)   (-)
main  0.333  685.00  3.27e9   -1.0  0.0   2.0   0.4   0.82  0.27
